@dayaseelamayadunne9319  ඒ සංවාදය  හොඳින්  අහලා 
තමයි  අදහස් ඉදිරිපත් කලේ.ඔබ  සහල්  වෙලෙන්දෙක් හෝ  ජාත්‍යන්තර  නියෝජිතයෙක් ද?මිල නියම කරන්න  කලින්  වගා කරලා  ඉන්න ඕන නේද .මිනිසුන්  බය කරන්න එපා.මෝඩයෝ 
කරන්නත් එපා.පුලුවන්  නම් නිස්සබ්දව බලා  ඉන්න .

@davidka8345  small scale agroecological production, is not only less and more meaningful work for the farmer, is also superior to large scale monocultures. The kind of farming we need to transition to is a lot closer to gardening and what peasants have always done which includes recycling biomass. I practice this stuff, it works and has revolutionary potential. 
In 2019 a high-level panel of experts at the FAO found small-scale agroecological farming  to be the scientific solution to our food security crisis and to climate change, it is also probably the world's largest political movement, why has the consumer in rich countries never ever heard about it? It's because there is a sophisticated and highly successful science denial machine which also happens to be very active on YouTube and has institutional authority in the academy and the media. 
So composting, which doesn't cost a damn thing besides a little sweat, is no problem for the kind of farming that works for socially just and environmentally sustainable agriculture

